== translate upgrade ==
MongoDB driver 6.21.0 and mongodb-legacy 6.1.3 are pinned. The deprecated legacy adapter bridges existing callbacks as a transition; future driver 7 migration requires converting these calls to Promises. Before starting against an existing database, set JINRO_MONGO_URI to its URI and run `node tool/migrate-blacklist-userid-index.js` to inspect, then `node tool/migrate-blacklist-userid-index.js --apply`. This required, idempotent migration replaces only the old unique blacklist.userid_1 index with a non-unique index; documents and the unique id index are preserved. Stop the app during this migration. Fresh databases already use the new index.

For a reproducible local database smoke test, start a dedicated MongoDB 8 instance bound only to 127.0.0.1 on an unused port, set JINRO_SMOKE_PORT to that port, then run `node tests/mongodb8-smoke.js`. The script uses a random guarded test database and removes only its own fixtures. It never reads config/app.coffee. Node 22 and MongoDB 8 were tested locally on Windows; the Linux Docker image and complete app/Redis/browser flow still require staging verification.
Historical tool/repair.js through tool/repair9.js target older driver APIs and are not deployment steps for this stack. tool/repair10-rebuild-userrawlogs-index.js uses the modern Promise API and an explicit JINRO_MONGO_URI; run database-changing tools only against the intended upgraded database during maintenance.
